Z||000017||frontal lobe||11-05-2001||01:31 AM||||Are the crummy department store bikes ok for just tooling around the city streets??  That's all I do with the kids, and with them growing (6, 9, 10 years old) I'd rather just buy cheap bikes for now since they are constantly out growing them.  On the other hand, I don't want to endanger them just to save some money.||||reg||1
Z||000018||WampusCat||11-05-2001||09:10 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by frontal lobe:<BR><B>Are the crummy department store bikes ok for just tooling around the city streets??  That's all I do with the kids, and with them growing (6, 9, 10 years old) I'd rather just buy cheap bikes for now since they are constantly out growing them.  On the other hand, I don't want to endanger them just to save some money.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Good question.  I don't think there's anything wrong with bargain store bikes if you're just cruisin' in town and most kids are so light that they aren't likely to pound one apart like a big person.  The problem comes when  people buy those things and think they can do serious trail riding with them.  <BR>Most bargain store bikes are made of mild steel cuz it's cheap.  To make the frame even close to stiff enough, it has to be very thick tubes, and thick=heavy.  Even with the thick, heavy frames though, you still get flex and that wears on parts and also can interfere with shifting.  Not all aluminum is created equal either.  Also, the parts on these things are cheap and heavy and just won't last or work as nice as even the lowest level of Shimano stuff.  So if you don't mind a bike that's 10 lbs. heavier than it needs to be and will likely wear out in a couple of years, and it won't be ridden off-road, then sure, get a Walmart special.  If any of your kids shows an interest in trail riding, I'd consider a name brand mtn. bike, maybe a used one if you can find one that small.  Check the 'net for tons of info on bicycle fit.  Huffy makes a darn good lawnmower, but...<BR>||||reg||1
